<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREA'S NLCF BUYS 77,000T CHINESE CORN - TRADERS.</title>
<headline>S.KOREA'S NLCF BUYS 77,000T CHINESE CORN - TRADERS.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's National Livestock Cooperatives Federation (NLCF) on Tuesday bought 77,000 tonnes of Chinese corn, traders said.  </p>
<p>They said the federation had originally sought 129,000 tonnes but had passed on 52,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p>    POSN   QNTY(T)  SELLER   ETA     PRICE/T  PORT</p>
<p>    One     52,000  passed</p>
<p>    Two     31,000  Cargill  Nov 15  $123.70  Inchon</p>
<p>    Three   21,000  Cargill  Nov 15  $123.70  Ulsan/Pusan</p>
<p>    Four    12,500  Daewoo   Oct 10  $127.30  Kunsan</p>
<p>    Five    12,500  Daewoo   Nov 15  $127.30  Kunsan</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
